<BaseLayout title="What We Believe">
<section class="hero" style="height:720px"><img src="/images/what-we-believe.jpg" srcset="/images/what-we-believe-1200.jpg 1200w, /images/what-we-believe.jpg 2576w" sizes="100vw" alt="What We Believe" style="object-position:center 45%;filter:grayscale(1) brightness(.5)" class="mono" fetchpriority="high" /><div class="veil"></div><SiteNav />
<div class="hero-c" style="top:259px;padding:0 24px"><span class="eb">The ground this altar stands on</span><h1 class="h1" style="margin-top:22px">What We Believe</h1><p class="it" style="margin:24px 0 0;max-width:680px;font-size:26px;line-height:1.4;color:#E6DFD0">A plain statement, so that every reader knows where we stand before we speak.</p></div></section>
<section class="sec paper"><div class="narrow" style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:0"><div class="rule rv" style="padding:44px 0;display:grid;grid-template-columns:90px minmax(0,1fr);gap:24px"><span class="num" style="color:#62372D">I</span><div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:14px"><h2 class="h2" style="font-size:44px">The Living God</h2><p class="body">We believe in one God, Father, Son and Holy Spirit, the Creator and Sustainer of all things. The universe is not a closed machine running on impersonal law; it is the sustained thought of its Maker. Its order is His faithfulness, and its laws are the consistent habits of a sovereign God.</p><span class="it mut" style="font-size:18px">For in Him all things hold together. · Colossians i · xvii</span></div></div><div class="rule rv" style="padding:44px 0;display:grid;grid-template-columns:90px minmax(0,1fr);gap:24px"><span class="num" style="color:#62372D">II</span><div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:14px"><h2 class="h2" style="font-size:44px">Christ, Crucified and Risen</h2><p class="body">We believe Jesus Christ is the Word made flesh, crucified for our sins and bodily raised on the third day. The resurrection is not an exception to reality but its deepest law: life, light and incorruptibility are what is ultimately real, and decay and death are temporary, destined to be overwritten.</p><span class="it mut" style="font-size:18px">Now is Christ risen from the dead, and become the firstfruits of them that slept. · 1 Corinthians xv · xx</span></div></div><div class="rule rv" style="padding:44px 0;display:grid;grid-template-columns:90px minmax(0,1fr);gap:24px"><span class="num" style="color:#62372D">III</span><div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:14px"><h2 class="h2" style="font-size:44px">The Surrendered Life</h2><p class="body">We believe true power is not self-exaltation but dying to the self to inherit divine authority. The longing to transcend human weakness is fulfilled only by the Holy Spirit, never by the fragile ego. We build without tools of pride.</p><span class="it mut" style="font-size:18px">I am crucified with Christ: nevertheless I live; yet not I, but Christ liveth in me. · Galatians ii · xx</span></div></div><div class="rule rv" style="padding:44px 0;display:grid;grid-template-columns:90px minmax(0,1fr);gap:24px"><span class="num" style="color:#62372D">IV</span><div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:14px"><h2 class="h2" style="font-size:44px">Image Bearers and Makers</h2><p class="body">We believe every person bears the image of God, and that human imagination is a reflection of the Imago Dei. Story and myth are not projections of the psyche; the Gospel is the True Myth, the archetype that stepped into time, flesh and stone. Every craft offered to Him is worship, and beauty belongs entirely to the Living God.</p><span class="it mut" style="font-size:18px">And I have filled him with the spirit of God, in wisdom, and in understanding, and in all manner of workmanship. · Exodus xxxi · iii</span></div></div><div class="rule rv" style="padding:44px 0;display:grid;grid-template-columns:90px minmax(0,1fr);gap:24px"><span class="num" style="color:#62372D">V</span><div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:14px"><h2 class="h2" style="font-size:44px">Discernment, Deliverance and the Prophetic</h2><p class="body">We believe the spiritual realm is real and that Christ has triumphed over every principality and power. We believe the Spirit still speaks, and that prophetic and discerning gifts are given to strengthen His people. Every word is weighed against Scripture and offered with humility; none is above testing.</p><span class="it mut" style="font-size:18px">Believe not every spirit, but try the spirits whether they are of God. · 1 John iv · i</span></div></div><div class="rule rv" style="padding:44px 0;display:grid;grid-template-columns:90px minmax(0,1fr);gap:24px"><span class="num" style="color:#62372D">VI</span><div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:14px"><h2 class="h2" style="font-size:44px">The Word</h2><p class="body">We receive the Holy Scriptures as the inspired Word of God. They judge every word on this site, our own first of all.</p><span class="it mut" style="font-size:18px">All scripture is given by inspiration of God. · 2 Timothy iii · xvi</span></div></div><div class="rule rv" style="padding:44px 0;display:grid;grid-template-columns:90px minmax(0,1fr);gap:24px"><span class="num" style="color:#62372D">VII</span><div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:14px"><h2 class="h2" style="font-size:44px">One Body</h2><p class="body">We are open to every denomination. The Church is one body in Christ, and we believe each tradition is a member of that body: a function given for the whole, and a roadway by which the gospel reaches people the others might not. We hold fast to the essentials of the faith, and in everything else we extend charity, honoring what God is doing through every part of His Church.</p><span class="it mut" style="font-size:18px">For as the body is one, and hath many members … so also is Christ. · 1 Corinthians xii · xii</span></div></div></div></section>
